---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="About | Dilanjan DK"
  description="Computational neuroscientist and researcher at Western University focused on clinical neuroimaging and scientific software."
>
  <header class="py-16 px-4 text-center bg-gradient-to-b from-surface to-background">
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-foreground">About Me</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-muted">Computational Neuroscientist — building reproducible tools for clinical neuroimaging.</p>
  </header>
  <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 py-16 md:py-20">
    <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-[0.7fr_1.3fr] gap-12 items-start">
      <div class="lg:sticky lg:top-24">
        <figure class="image-frame overflow-hidden rounded-[1.5rem] border border-border bg-card rotate-[-2deg]">
          <img src="/assets/images/Dilanjan.png" alt="Portrait of Dilanjan Diyabalanage" class="w-full aspect-[4/5] object-cover object-top" width="749" height="757" loading="eager" />
          <figcaption class="px-4 py-3 text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-muted">Dilanjan Diyabalanage / computational neuroscience</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="image-frame mt-8 overflow-hidden rounded-[1.5rem] border border-border bg-card rotate-[2deg]">
          <img src="/assets/images/aboutme.jpg" alt="Illustrated portrait of Dilanjan hugging a happy dog" class="w-full aspect-square object-cover" width="460" height="460" loading="lazy" />
          <figcaption class="px-4 py-3 text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-muted">Outside the lab</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <p class="section-kicker mt-10">What I work on</p>
        <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-foreground">From brain data to dependable tools.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="space-y-10">
        <div class="space-y-4 text-lg leading-relaxed">
          <p class="text-foreground/90">I'm Dilanjan Diyabalanage, a computational neuroscientist and researcher at Western University. I work across clinical neuroimaging, EEG analysis, machine learning, and scientific software.</p>
          <p class="text-foreground/80">My focus is turning difficult brain-data problems into methods that are reproducible, inspectable, and practical for researchers and collaborators.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
          {[
            ['Clinical neuroimaging', 'fMRI workflows, preprocessing, feature extraction, and analysis for neuroscience research.'],
            ['Machine learning', 'Physics-informed models and deep-learning methods for health and biomedical data.'],
            ['EEG analysis', 'Source reconstruction, dynamical features, and computational approaches to neural signals.'],
            ['Scientific software', 'Open-source Python tools, containers, workflows, documentation, and reproducible delivery.'],
          ].map(([title, detail]) => (
            <article class="rounded-[1.25rem] border border-border bg-card p-5 hover:-translate-y-1 hover:border-primary/60 transition-all">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-foreground">{title}</h3>
              <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">{detail}</p>
            </article>
          ))}
        </div>
        <div class="border-t border-border pt-6 space-y-4">
          <p class="text-foreground/90"><strong>Mission:</strong> Make neuroimaging research more reproducible, scalable, and useful through reliable scientific software.</p>
          <p class="text-foreground/80">Contact: <a href="mailto:ddiyabal@uwo.ca" class="text-primary hover:underline">ddiyabal@uwo.ca</a> | <a href="https://github.com/DilanjanDK7" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-primary hover:underline">GitHub</a> | <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/dilanjandk" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-primary hover:underline">LinkedIn</a> | <a href="https://orcid.org/0009-0004-6672-2636" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-primary hover:underline">ORCID</a></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
